  "title": "Credential suffixes survive cuts inside ANSI sequences",
  "file": "src/gates/output.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A gate prints a registered credential that has a color escape sequence in the middle of it, and the runner's output cap cuts right at that sequence. The leftover formatting text uses up the fixed overlap that gets dropped, so the last part of the credential stays in the stored output and the model feedback.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun $TMPDIR/adj/c.ts $PWD  (registerCredential('T1', s); redactGateStreams('[38;2;123;123;123m' + s.slice(2), '', {stdoutTruncated:true}).stdout)",
    "output": "C1 \"ry-credential-421\""
   },
   "evidence": "output.ts:33-36: `const overlap = Math.max(0, ...registeredCredentials().map((secret) => secret.length - 1)); ... redactGateOutput(stdout).slice(cuts.stdoutTruncated ? overlap : 0)`. The overlap is counted in normalized characters, but the cut was made on raw text. When the ESC byte is cut off, stripVTControlCharacters leaves the rest of the sequence in place, and that rest eats part of the overlap. Gates also run with NO_COLOR=1, and the credential has to contain the escape sequence itself, so this input is unusual."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A check prints a colored credential in sufficiently long output. When the runner cuts through the formatting sequence, part of the credential survives sanitization and enters the gate result.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"$TMPDIR/adjudicate-103.ts\" C1",
    "output": "{\"direct\":\"ry-credential-421\",\"gateOutput\":\"ry-credential-421zzz\"}"
   },
   "evidence": "The probe exercised real runGates subprocess handling with a test confinement backend. Its 64,000-character runner tail begins with '[38;2;123;123;123m' followed by the credential minus its first two characters, then removable ANSI padding. HEAD uses 'redactGateOutput(stdout).slice(cuts.stdoutTruncated ? overlap : 0)'. The incomplete formatting prefix survives normalization and consumes the overlap, leaving credential bytes. Base retained the raw final 6,000 characters; for this fixture those contain only trailing formatting, so this particular disclosure is newly introduced."
  }
 },
